Rule 1 (input tensor must have at least two dimensions)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2
>>
Rule 2 (diagonal offset must be within matrix dimension bounds)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2 < shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) ∧ v_2 > 0 - shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 3 (input tensor must have at least 2 dimensions and all dimensions must be positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
>>
Rule 4 (offset must be within the bounds of the matrix dimensions to yield a non-empty diagonal)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ (if v_2 ≥ 0 then v_2 < shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) else 0 - v_2 < shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2))
>>
Rule 5 (offset must allow a non-empty diagonal within the matrix slices)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2 + shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2) > 0 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) - v_2 > 0
>>
Rule 6 (tensor must be at least 2-dimensional with a valid numeric data type)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≥ 0 ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 10
>>
Rule 7 (matrix slices must be square matrices)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1) = shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 8 (non-negative offset for super-diagonals must be strictly less than the column dimension)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2 ≥ 0 ∧ v_2 < shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 1)
>>
Rule 9 (non-positive offset for sub-diagonals must be strictly less than the row dimension in magnitude)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : int} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 2 ∧ v_2 ≤ 0 ∧ 0 - v_2 < shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - 2)
>>
Rule 10 (batched matrix input has at least 3 dimensions with all batch dimensions positive)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 3 ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 3] : shape(v_1, i) > 0
